                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8a8a7fed-5c8c-406b-b990-8a3b661bf2a6",
                        "entry_id": "e4110400-002a-3fee-89cd-d4b04bdd2afe",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "сенова́лах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                        "entry_id": "e4110400-002a-3fee-89cd-d4b04bdd2afe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сарай, навес или помещение над конюшней, скотным двором для хранения сена"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f8bb8be-44c8-4231-aa9c-95123b399f05",
                                "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                                "text": "Проживал он летом в клети, позади курятника, а зимой в предбаннике; в сильные морозы ночевал на сеновале."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32f4ac6e-afc5-4eb4-8e0a-313cec47a3e5",
                                "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                                "text": "Он бросился от неё к сеновалу, с намерением взобраться туда по крутой лестнице, и едва она поспевала дойти до сеновала, как уж надо было спешить разрушать его замыслы влезть на голубятню, проникнуть на скотный двор и, чего боже сохрани!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc11aa4d-7b5d-4ad6-80fa-bd6fb1c82d8a",
                                "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                                "text": "С другой стороны дома, обращённой к дворам, ей было видно всё, что делается на большом дворе, в людской, в кухне, на сеновале, в конюшне, в погребах."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15c9406e-e661-463d-ac82-e95d2aaf18cf",
                                "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                                "text": "Люди в кухне поужинали и расходились по двору спать: кто под сараи, кто к амбарам, кто на высокие душистые сеновалы."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c769e49-0e2a-4371-8001-5f864b06d23d",
                                "sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                                "text": "Сперва в утайку заговаривали, что она ходит к нему на сеновал, а потом говор пошёл чуть не открыто."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eae28b11-4e6b-46b9-ba0f-b96b07068a8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e4110400-002a-3fee-89cd-d4b04bdd2afe",
                        "source_sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                        "target_lang_word": "hayloft",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hayloft",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc82b058-c648-3f72-aa5c-2d8ace63e519",
                                        "entry_id": "4282978e-cc4d-313b-9a29-16d52f37300f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The upper storey of a barn used for storing hay."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8adb71c2-a78d-46c1-86f6-7e7dc29eb57a",
                                                "sense_id": "dc82b058-c648-3f72-aa5c-2d8ace63e519",
                                                "text": "\"I went into the stable first to see to the horse, and found him neighing and waiting for his hay, so I went up into the hay-loft for an armful[.]\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5942503d-5061-460e-a24a-44be6812b24d",
                        "source_entry_id": "e4110400-002a-3fee-89cd-d4b04bdd2afe",
                        "source_sense_id": "eed87086-82ab-3d32-827c-c3cdd9406205",
                        "target_lang_word": "mow",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecf5f78c-2789-3f01-9d74-06111dd55f98",
                                        "entry_id": "3453a5cb-8c83-3572-b4f7-3a86d110dd88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut down grass or crops."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee3a6dc8-59bd-4c40-8384-8cc9d6771dbc",
                                                "sense_id": "ecf5f78c-2789-3f01-9d74-06111dd55f98",
                                                "text": "He mowed the lawn every few weeks in the summer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5dd77eb-3efb-3bfe-81d9-d6fa0f80bfe7",
                                        "entry_id": "3453a5cb-8c83-3572-b4f7-3a86d110dd88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut down or slaughter in great numbers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "often",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "859b3dc5-788b-4dfb-9cba-efaf0c1d7d3d",
                                                "sense_id": "a5dd77eb-3efb-3bfe-81d9-d6fa0f80bfe7",
                                                "text": "In the afternoon they attacked again, in close formation: our artillery mowed them, but they came on and on, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7101320-425c-45ff-a500-57bae4518d65",
                                                "sense_id": "a5dd77eb-3efb-3bfe-81d9-d6fa0f80bfe7",
                                                "text": "On the one hand, we had a scenario where, effectively, the American admiral just went \"You know what, all the destroyers attack\", at which point they mowed through the Japanese destroyers like a Grim Reaper through a harvest of very, very dead gorn, especially with the Brooklyns in support."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "172926c6-f26f-3e9c-b295-9de85ae51541",
                                        "entry_id": "83f46dda-4aa7-3908-bfeb-a4b9d8c0f04f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of mowing (a garden, grass, etc.)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6b62b13-b221-4b4a-aa06-61582b782880",
                                                "sense_id": "172926c6-f26f-3e9c-b295-9de85ae51541",
                                                "text": "The lawn hasn't had a mow for a couple of months, so it's like a jungle out there!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3aa03748-d048-3b60-8bfd-c2ce980571e9",
                                        "entry_id": "83f46dda-4aa7-3908-bfeb-a4b9d8c0f04f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shot played with a sweeping or scythe-like motion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c182851-8d15-4ff9-a7ad-f7d168cfabd0",
                                                "sense_id": "3aa03748-d048-3b60-8bfd-c2ce980571e9",
                                                "text": "I consider it would engender a stiff, tame, cautious mode of play, with only now and then a mow, or a chopping hit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b0328b8-fbcc-4aad-80fd-271274091c28",
                                                "sense_id": "3aa03748-d048-3b60-8bfd-c2ce980571e9",
                                                "text": "At times, they seemed to be playing an especially orgiastic version of Stick Cricket, all computerised mows over midwicket and 30 off the over."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0f09c88-c6a8-30e1-aa03-ce00cb84ff3f",
                                        "entry_id": "9dff946c-ff70-3f3a-93e6-e6833058b435",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A scornful grimace; a wry face."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab4ecb0f-ed86-4d02-abeb-8f0fea1bffb8",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f09c88-c6a8-30e1-aa03-ce00cb84ff3f",
                                                "text": "Those that paint them dying […] delineate the prisoners spitting in their executioners faces, and making mowes at them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "967b5913-229e-4259-8202-67406e41adad",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f09c88-c6a8-30e1-aa03-ce00cb84ff3f",
                                                "text": "Make mows at him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e62d7484-e127-3204-90dc-489019be9942",
                                        "entry_id": "606ce017-14fe-33da-89a4-73c71858ed78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make grimaces, mock."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78ea7f76-6bd2-4228-a9ec-ad9e0d9140cf",
                                                "sense_id": "e62d7484-e127-3204-90dc-489019be9942",
                                                "text": "For every trifle are they set upon me: / Sometime like apes that mow and chatter at me, / And after bite me;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e604ba3-adda-403b-8a36-416d1b37e259",
                                                "sense_id": "e62d7484-e127-3204-90dc-489019be9942",
                                                "text": "Nodding, becking, and mowing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2353c34f-25c6-4a6d-b44d-4fd987375d8a",
                                                "sense_id": "e62d7484-e127-3204-90dc-489019be9942",
                                                "text": "He mowed at me, and, bowing with ironical politeness, pointed to the house."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mow",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
